        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "slo:error_budget_remaining:ratio{provider=~\"$provider\", slo=~\"$slo\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{provider}} · {{slo}}",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "format": "time_series",
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "description": "",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 20
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\n#### How these SLOs work\nFollowing *The Site Reliability Workbook* (ch. 2 & 5). Every SLO is one series `slo:sli_good:ratio{slo, provider}`;\ngeneric recording rules turn it into error ratios over many windows, burn rates and the remaining budget.\n\n| SLI | good event | objective (30 d) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **availability** | scrape of the JSON API succeeded | 99.5 % |\n| **latency** | synthetic probe OK **and** < 1 s | 99 % |\n| **freshness** | data age < 5 min (USGS) / 30 min (weather) / 2 h (air) | 99 % |\n\n**Multi-window, multi-burn-rate alerts**\n\n| severity | burn rate | long / short window | budget used |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| page | 14.4× | 1 h / 5 m | 2 % |\n| page | 6× | 6 h / 30 m | 5 % |\n| ticket | 3× | 1 d / 2 h | 10 % |\n| ticket | 1× | 3 d / 6 h | 10 % |\n\nBurn rate 1 = budget lasts exactly 30 days. Policy: `docs/error-budget-policy.md`.\n"
      },
      "transparent": false
    },
